                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239519868",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198005738407",
                            "num_reviews": 68,
                            "playtime_forever": 350,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 350,
                            "playtime_at_review": 350,
                            "last_played": 1793983410
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game is severely underappreciated because it's not like other Ice-Pick Lodge titles. There's no Pathologic levels of philosophy or strong engaging gameplay, yet it is still a very solid narrative adventure with at least couple of moments that made me go \"Wow, yeah, this is really well-thought\", even though I had my fair share of narrative adventures.\nObviously will be more touching to post-soviet people, as the nostalgia-bait layer of this game serves to them, but will still be an interesting experience for everybody else.\nAnd yeah, it is obviously a tear-jerker, but not the kind that has nothing behind it. Good game!",
